(GOVERNMENT OF INDIA - MINISTRY OF FINANCE - DEPARTMENT OF FINANCIAL SERVICES) Tj
T*
(OPERATIONAL GUIDELINES: STAND-UP INDIA SCHEME \(STANDUP-INDIA\) / SIDBI / SCHEDULED COMMERCIAL BANKS) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Overview & Objective:) Tj
T*
(Bank loans between Rs. 10 Lakh and Rs. 1 Crore to at least one Scheduled Caste) Tj
T*
(\(SC\) or Scheduled Tribe \(ST\) borrower and at least one woman borrower per) Tj
T*
(bank branch for setting up greenfield enterprises.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Eligibility Criteria:) Tj
T*
(1. SC/ST and/or woman entrepreneurs above 18 years of age.) Tj
T*
(2. Loans under the scheme are available only for greenfield projects \(the) Tj
T*
(   first-time venture of the beneficiary in manufacturing, services, agri-) Tj
T*
(   allied activities, or trading\).) Tj
T*
(3. In case of non-individual enterprises, 51% of the shareholding and) Tj
T*
(   controlling stake must be held by either SC/ST and/or women) Tj
T*
(   entrepreneur.) Tj
T*
(4. Borrower should not be in default to any bank or financial institution.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Financial Assistance and Subsidy:) Tj
T*
(1. Composite loan \(term loan and working capital\) between Rs. 10 Lakh and Rs. 1) Tj
T*
(   Crore covering up to 85% of total project cost.) Tj
T*
(3. Maximum financial assistance cap is Rs 1.00 Crore per unit.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Mandatory Documents Checklist:) Tj
T*
(1. Identity and Address Proof of applicant/promoters) Tj
T*
(2. Caste Certificate \(for SC/ST category\)) Tj
T*
(3. Proof of Woman Ownership \(CA Certificate or ROC Shareholding pattern) Tj
T*
(   showing ? 51% equity\)) Tj
T*
(4. Detailed Project Report \(DPR\)) Tj
T*
(5. GST / Udyam registration) Tj
T*
(6. Lease deed / land allotment papers for business premises) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Application Procedure:) Tj
T*
(1. Mode: Online via Stand-Up India Portal or Bank Branches) Tj
T*
(2. Official Portal: https://www.standupmitra.in/) Tj
T*
